<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\phi : \calX \rightarrow \calY $ be a geometric morphism such that $\phi _{\ast }$ is fully faithful. By Proposition <a href="/tag/7751D7" data-tag="7751D7">5.5.6.28</a> and Remark <a href="/tag/AB6A8B" data-tag="AB6A8B">6.5.1.4</a>, it will suffice to prove the lemma in the case where $\calX = \calY $. We may therefore assume that $\calY $ is an $\infty $-category of presheaves. In this case, homotopy groups and truncations are computed pointwise. Thus we may reduce to the case $\calX = \SSet $, where the conclusion follows from classical homotopy theory. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
